  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x$ are given by\n\n$$\nx=n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=2\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-\\frac{\\pi }{6} & =n\\pi  \\\\ 2x & =n\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{12}+\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
